<root>
  <h2>Text</h2>
  <section>
    <p style="color:var(--fg-muted);font-size:0.875rem;margin:0 0 0.75rem">
      Typography primitive powered by a Rust port of
      <a href="https://github.com/chenglou/pretext" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">pretext</a>.
      Measures text with Canvas <code>measureText()</code> so
      truncation lands on an exact grapheme boundary and
      <code>data-truncated</code> tells your CSS when overflow
      happened.
    </p>

    <div class="text-demo-block">
      <div class="text-demo-label">Baseline</div>
      <pine-text class="text-demo-body">
        The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.
      </pine-text>
    </div>

    <div class="text-demo-block">
      <div class="text-demo-label">Truncate to 2 lines</div>
      <div class="text-demo-frame" style="max-width:22rem">
        <pine-text lines="2" class="text-demo-body">
          Typography primitives benefit from measurement-backed
          layout because CSS alone cannot tell you how many lines
          a paragraph actually wraps into, which is what you need
          for honest truncation, balanced headlines, and
          fit-to-width effects.
        </pine-text>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="text-demo-block">
      <div class="text-demo-label">Live reflow</div>
      <pine-slider-root min="120"
                        max="480"
                        step="10"
                        pp-model:value="width">
        <pine-slider-track>
          <pine-slider-range></pine-slider-range>
        </pine-slider-track>
        <pine-slider-thumb></pine-slider-thumb>
      </pine-slider-root>
      <p style="margin:0.5rem 0;font-size:0.875rem">
        Width: <strong pp-text="width + 'px'"></strong>
      </p>
      <div class="text-demo-frame" :style="'max-width:' + width + 'px'">
        <pine-text lines="3"
                   :max-width="width"
                   class="text-demo-body">
          Drag the slider to watch the paragraph reflow. The layout
          engine re-runs on every width change and the
          <code>data-truncated</code> attribute flips whenever the
          paragraph no longer fits in three lines.
        </pine-text>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="text-demo-block">
      <div class="text-demo-label">Soft hyphens</div>
      <div class="text-demo-frame" style="max-width:10rem">
        <pine-text class="text-demo-body">
          super&shy;califragi&shy;listic&shy;expiali&shy;docious
        </pine-text>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</root>
